[{"id":"adv-edit-010","type":"error_correction","prompt":"The soup is tasting too salty today.","answer":"The soup tastes too salty today.","explanation_ru":"Taste описывает свойство супа и потому используется в Simple; Continuous означал бы намеренное пробование человеком.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#11-stative-verbs-категории-и-исключения"],"cefr_estimate":"B2"},{"id":"adv-edit-011","type":"error_correction","prompt":"Until 5 p.m. tomorrow, the panel will have reached a decision.","answer":"By 5 p.m. tomorrow, the panel will have reached a decision.","explanation_ru":"By задаёт крайний срок достижения результата; until описывало бы продолжение процесса до момента.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#7-by-и-untiltill"],"cefr_estimate":"B2"},{"id":"adv-edit-012","type":"error_correction","prompt":"Rarely I have seen an argument collapse so quickly under scrutiny.","answer":"Rarely have I seen an argument collapse so quickly under scrutiny.","explanation_ru":"После вынесенного в начало rarely требуется инверсия; Present Perfect сохраняет связь опыта с настоящим.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#18-маркированные-и-продвинутые-употребления","content/tenses/02-present.md#present-perfect-simple"],"cefr_estimate":"C1"},{"id":"adv-discourse-001","type":"discourse_choice","prompt":"Choose the ending that keeps the narrator inside the past scene: The corridor was empty. Somewhere below, a door slammed. Lena checked her watch. She realised that ...","answer":"she had less than a minute left","explanation_ru":"Точка отсчёта рассказа остаётся в прошлом, поэтому состояние, осознанное Леной тогда, оформляется Past Simple.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема","content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#19-как-разбирать-неоднозначное-предложение"],"cefr_estimate":"C1","options":["she has less than a minute left","she had less than a minute left","she will have less than a minute left"],"correct_option_index":1,"review_note_ru":"Past forms maintain the deictic centre inside the remembered scene; has would abruptly return to the speaker's present."},{"id":"adv-discourse-002","type":"discourse_choice","prompt":"Which version presents the research as ongoing rather than as a completed body of work?","answer":"For the past decade, the lab has been mapping coastal erosion in the region.","explanation_ru":"Обе формы возможны, но Continuous сильнее удерживает внимание на продолжающемся процессе.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#3-perfect-simple-и-perfect-continuous-результат-или-деятельность","content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#19-как-разбирать-неоднозначное-предложение"],"cefr_estimate":"C1","options":["For the past decade, the lab has mapped coastal erosion in the region.","For the past decade, the lab has been mapping coastal erosion in the region."],"correct_option_index":1,"review_note_ru":"The Continuous version foregrounds the continuing activity; the Simple version packages the work more readily as an achieved record."},{"id":"adv-discourse-003","type":"discourse_choice","prompt":"A biography is being edited in 2026. Which sentence unambiguously says that the subject no longer lives in Paris?","answer":"She lived in Paris for twenty years.","explanation_ru":"Задача проверяет не маркер for, а открытую или закрытую временную рамку.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#2-perfect-и-past-до-сейчас-или-законченное-прошлое","content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#19-как-разбирать-неоднозначное-предложение"],"cefr_estimate":"C1","options":["She has lived in Paris for twenty years.","She lived in Paris for twenty years.","She has been living in Paris for twenty years."],"correct_option_index":1,"review_note_ru":"Past Simple closes the period. Both Present Perfect options normally connect the residence to the present."},{"id":"adv-discourse-004","type":"discourse_choice","prompt":"Which sentence most naturally reports an expected event that was later cancelled?","answer":"The minister was to address the conference, but the visit was cancelled.","explanation_ru":"Was to ясно представляет официально запланированное будущее из прошлого; продолжение отменяет реализацию плана.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#19-как-разбирать-неоднозначное-предложение"],"cefr_estimate":"C1","options":["The minister would address the conference, but the visit was cancelled.","The minister was to address the conference, but the visit was cancelled.","The minister addressed the conference, but the visit was cancelled."],"correct_option_index":1,"review_note_ru":"Was to is suited to an official arrangement viewed from the past and does not itself assert fulfilment."},{"id":"adv-discourse-005","type":"discourse_choice","prompt":"Which version is best for a formal written review that shifts into a vivid scene-by-scene summary?","answer":"The narrator enters the archive and finds the ledger.","explanation_ru":"Настоящее время здесь не датирует событие настоящим, а меняет повествовательную перспективу.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#18-маркированные-и-продвинутые-употребления"],"cefr_estimate":"C2","options":["The narrator had entered the archive and had found the ledger.","The narrator enters the archive and finds the ledger.","The narrator has entered the archive and found the ledger yesterday."],"correct_option_index":1,"review_note_ru":"The historical present is a conventional marked choice for vivid summaries; the third option conflicts with yesterday."},{"id":"adv-discourse-006","type":"discourse_choice","prompt":"The evidence is indirect but strong. Which sentence uses Future Perfect epistemically rather than temporally?","answer":"The courier will have delivered the parcel by now; the tracking page shows it at the local depot.","explanation_ru":"Future Perfect может выражать уверенное предположение о прошлом относительно настоящего, а не только завершение к будущему сроку.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/04-future.md#future-perfect-simple-will-have--v3","content/tenses/05-contrasts-and-pitfalls.md#18-маркированные-и-продвинутые-употребления"],"cefr_estimate":"C2","options":["By Friday, the courier will have delivered the parcel.","The courier will have delivered the parcel by now; the tracking page shows it at the local depot.","The courier will be delivering the parcel at noon."],"correct_option_index":1,"review_note_ru":"By now plus supporting evidence makes will have delivered an inference about a probably completed event."},{"id":"adv-cloze-001","type":"context_cloze","prompt":"When the product team {{1:meet}} on Monday morning, they discovered that the supplier {{2:not deliver}} a critical component. They {{3:expect}} it the previous Friday and {{4:plan}} to begin testing over the weekend. By then, the engineers {{5:work}} on the release for six months. The director said the company {{6:postpone}} the launch if the part did not arrive by noon. It finally {{7:turn up}} at eleven, just as the team {{8:prepare}} the delay notice.","answer":["met","had not delivered","had expected","had planned","had been working","would postpone","turned up","was preparing"],"explanation_ru":"Past Simple ведёт события, Perfect-формы восстанавливают предысторию, would задаёт будущее из прошлой точки, Past Continuous показывает прерванный процесс.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"],"cefr_estimate":"C1","title":"The delayed launch","blanks":[{"id":"adv-cloze-001-b1","answer":"met","accepted_answers":["met"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"]},{"id":"adv-cloze-001-b2","answer":"had not delivered","accepted_answers":["had not delivered"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"]},{"id":"adv-cloze-001-b3","answer":"had expected","accepted_answers":["had expected"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"]},{"id":"adv-cloze-001-b4","answer":"had planned","accepted_answers":["had planned"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"]},{"id":"adv-cloze-001-b5","answer":"had been working","accepted_answers":["had been working"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"]},{"id":"adv-cloze-001-b6","answer":"would postpone","accepted_answers":["would postpone"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"]},{"id":"adv-cloze-001-b7","answer":"turned up","accepted_answers":["turned up"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"]},{"id":"adv-cloze-001-b8","answer":"was preparing","accepted_answers":["was preparing"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/03-past.md#past-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-simple","content/tenses/03-past.md#past-perfect-continuous","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-in-the-past","content/tenses/03-past.md#повествовательная-схема"]}]},{"id":"adv-cloze-002","type":"context_cloze","prompt":"The observatory {{1:open}} its new wing next April according to the official programme. By then, researchers {{2:collect}} atmospheric data at the site for twenty-five years and {{3:complete}} the first full regional model. At this time next May, visiting scientists {{4:use}} the new instruments. The director {{5:meet}} the first group on 3 May; the appointment is already fixed. As soon as they {{6:arrive}}, technicians {{7:give}} them a safety briefing. The project team believes the expansion {{8:transform}} the centre's work.","answer":["opens","will have been collecting","will have completed","will be using","is meeting","arrive","will give","will transform"],"explanation_ru":"Текст требует различить расписание, договорённость, процесс и результат к будущей точке, а также форму в придаточном времени.","rule_refs":["content/tenses/04-future.md#present-simple-для-будущего","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-perfect-continuous-will-have-been--v-ing","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-perfect-simple-will-have--v3","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-continuous-will-be--v-ing","content/tenses/04-future.md#present-continuous-для-будущего","content/tenses/04-future.md#future-time-clauses"],"cefr_estimate":"C1","title":"A long-term forecast","blanks":[{"id":"adv-cloze-002-b1","answer":"opens","accepted_answers":["opens"],"rule_refs":["content/tenses/04-future.md#present-simple-для-будуще